---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Ransomware deletes the backups" hint="An attacker with stolen administrator credentials encrypts the database and then deletes every backup it can reach. Change how the backups are protected and see which restore points survive.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The <b>default</b> has a copy in another region, but the storage is <b>open</b> and the copy is a <b>mirror</b>: the attacker's deletes are replicated, so <b>no restore point survives</b>. Having two regions is not the same as having an independent copy.</li>
    <li>Set the other-region copy to <b>an independent locked copy</b>: the clean points survive, but the restore comes from the other region and takes <b>5 hours</b>, which misses a 4 hour target. Also switching the protection to a <b>compliance lock</b> restores from the primary in <b>2 hours</b>.</li>
    <li>With <b>an independent locked copy</b> and the <b>compliance lock</b> still set, set the <b>time the attacker stayed hidden</b> to <b>30 days</b> with 30 days of retention. Even the lock cannot help: the last clean backup has <b>already expired</b>, and every backup that remains holds encrypted data.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg bkb" data-bkb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Primary backup storage <select class="pg-in" data-prot>
        <option value="open" selected>same account, deletable</option>
        <option value="separate">separate account, no delete from production</option>
        <option value="lock">separate account, compliance lock</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Copy in another region <select class="pg-in" data-copy>
        <option value="none">none</option>
        <option value="mirror" selected>mirror (deletes are replicated)</option>
        <option value="locked">independent locked copy</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Days the attacker stayed hidden <input type="range" min="1" max="30" value="9" data-dwell /> <b data-dwellval></b></label>
      <label>Retention (days) <input type="range" min="7" max="42" value="30" data-ret /> <b data-retval></b></label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-adm /> Attacker also phished the backup account's admin</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-down /> Primary region is down during recovery</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Primary region vault</h3><div class="bk-strip" data-s1 role="img" aria-label="Primary vault backups, 42 days"></div><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Copy in another region</h3><div class="bk-strip" data-s2 role="img" aria-label="Other region backups, 42 days"></div><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Restore</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Retention against the hidden days</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note"><span class="bk-key bk-clean"></span> clean backup <span class="bk-key bk-bad"></span> backup of encrypted data <span class="bk-key bk-gone"></span> deleted or missing <span class="bk-key bk-old"></span> expired. Each strip shows the last 42 days, with today at the right.</p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: one backup a day, and the attacker's data is encrypted from the first hidden day, so every backup from then on holds encrypted data. On the last day the attacker deletes everything that the stolen login reaches. With a compliance lock nothing can be deleted before the retention ends. A mirror is in the same account as the primary, so it is deleted too. A restore takes 2 hours from the primary region and 5 hours from the other region, which includes the download, and the target is 4 hours. Changes since the last clean backup are lost, as the log is also encrypted or deleted.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-bkb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const DAYS = 42; const RTO = 4; const LOCAL_H = 2; const REMOTE_H = 5;
    type P = { prot: string; copy: string; dwell: number; ret: number; adm: boolean; down: boolean };
    // Pure model: which backups survive the attack in each place, and what a restore then looks like.
    function simulate(p: P) {
      const first = DAYS - 1 - p.dwell; // first day with encrypted data
      const primSurvive = p.prot === 'lock' || (p.prot === 'separate' && !p.adm);
      const remSurvive = p.copy === 'locked' || (p.copy === 'mirror' && primSurvive);
      const strip = (survive: boolean, exists: boolean) => Array.from({ length: DAYS }, (_, i) => {
        if (!exists || !survive) return 'gone';
        if (DAYS - 1 - i > p.ret) return 'old';
        return i >= first ? 'bad' : 'clean';
      });
      const prim = strip(primSurvive, true); const rem = strip(remSurvive, p.copy !== 'none');
      const cleanOf = (s: string[]) => s.filter((c) => c === 'clean').length;
      const primUse = !p.down && cleanOf(prim) > 0; const remUse = cleanOf(rem) > 0;
      const ok = primUse || remUse; const hours = primUse ? LOCAL_H : REMOTE_H;
      const needRet = p.dwell + 1;
      return { prim, rem, primUse, remUse, ok, hours, lost: p.dwell + 1, needRet, retOk: p.ret >= needRet, primSurvive, remSurvive };
    }
    // Build the strips once, then only change the classes.
    const cells = [1, 2].map((k) => Array.from({ length: DAYS }, () => { const c = document.createElement('span'); q(`[data-s${k}]`).append(c); return c; }));
    function draw() {
      const p: P = { prot: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-prot]').value, copy: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-copy]').value, dwell: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-dwell]').value), ret: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-ret]').value), adm: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-adm]').checked, down: q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-down]').checked };
      q('[data-dwellval]').textContent = String(p.dwell); q('[data-retval]').textContent = String(p.ret);
      const r = simulate(p);
      [r.prim, r.rem].forEach((s, k) => { s.forEach((st, i) => (cells[k][i].className = `bk-${st}`)); });
      const count = (s: string[], t: string) => s.filter((c) => c === t).length;
      const cp = count(r.prim, 'clean'); const cr = count(r.rem, 'clean');
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = r.primSurvive ? `${cp} clean points` : 'all deleted';
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = p.down ? 'the region is down, so nothing here can be read' : r.primSurvive ? (p.prot === 'lock' ? 'the lock refused every delete' : 'the production login cannot delete here') : p.prot === 'open' ? 'deleted with the stolen production login' : 'deleted with the phished backup admin';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = p.copy === 'none' ? 'no copy' : r.remSurvive ? `${cr} clean points` : 'all deleted';
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = p.copy === 'none' ? 'only one place holds the backups' : p.copy === 'mirror' ? (r.remSurvive ? 'it is a mirror, and the primary survived' : 'the deletes were replicated to the mirror') : 'separate account, locked, never replicated';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = r.ok ? `${r.hours} hours, from the ${r.primUse ? 'primary' : 'other'} region` : 'nothing to restore from';
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = r.ok ? `${r.lost} days of changes lost; ${r.hours <= RTO ? 'meets' : 'misses'} the ${RTO} hour target` : 'the only choices are to pay or to start again';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${p.ret} days kept, ${r.needRet} needed`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = r.retOk ? 'the last clean backup is still inside retention' : `the last clean backup is ${r.needRet} days old and has expired`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.primSurvive && cp > 0 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', p.copy === 'none' ? 'var(--border)' : r.remSurvive && cr > 0 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', r.ok ? (r.hours <= RTO ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--accent)') : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', r.retOk ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').classList.toggle('off', p.copy === 'none');
      q('[data-s1]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Primary vault, ${DAYS} days: ${cp} clean, ${count(r.prim, 'bad')} encrypted, ${count(r.prim, 'gone')} deleted, ${count(r.prim, 'old')} expired`);
      q('[data-s2]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Other region, ${DAYS} days: ${cr} clean, ${count(r.rem, 'bad')} encrypted, ${count(r.rem, 'gone')} deleted or missing, ${count(r.rem, 'old')} expired`);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]');
      const bad = !r.ok || r.hours > RTO; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      let why = '';
      if (!r.ok) {
        if (!r.retOk && (r.primSurvive || r.remSurvive)) why = `Every backup that is left holds encrypted data: the attacker was hidden for ${p.dwell} days, so the last clean backup was ${r.needRet} days old, and retention is only ${p.ret}. Keep at least ${r.needRet} days (more for important data).`;
        else if (p.copy === 'mirror' && !r.primSurvive) why = 'The mirror in another region did not help: it is a copy of the primary, deletes included, so the attacker removed both. Keep the second copy independent and locked.';
        else if (p.down && r.primSurvive && p.copy === 'none') why = 'The backups are safe in the primary region, but the region is down and there is no copy anywhere else.';
        else why = `No restore point survives: ${p.prot === 'open' ? 'the stolen production login deleted the backups' : 'the phished backup-account admin deleted them'}${p.copy === 'none' ? ', and there is no other copy' : ''}. Only a compliance lock, or a copy the attacker cannot reach, stops that.`;
      } else {
        why = `${r.primUse ? 'Restoring from the primary region' : 'Restoring from the other region'} takes ${r.hours} hours and loses ${r.lost} days of changes.${r.hours > RTO ? ` That misses the ${RTO} hour target, since the download from the other region adds time. A compliance lock in the primary region, with the region up, restores faster.` : ''}`;
      }
      out.textContent = why;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .bk-strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(42, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; height: 22px; }
  .playground .bk-strip span { display: block; border-radius: 1px; border: 1px solid transparent; }
  .playground .bk-clean { background: var(--good); }
  .playground .bk-bad { background: var(--bad); }
  .playground .bk-gone { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--muted) !important; }
  .playground .bk-old { background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border) !important; }
  .playground .bk-key { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 2px; vertical-align: -1px; margin-left: 8px; }
  .playground .bk-key:first-child { margin-left: 0; }
</style>
